Translation patch: `From<..> for Params` (`#[verify::start_from]`)

Change: Adds `#[verify::start_from]` to the impls `From<&T>`, `From<Vec<T>>`, `From<Vec<(N, V)>>`, `From<()>` and (inside `into_params_impl!`) the twelve tuple impls `From<(A, ..)>` for `Params` (the mechanism of patch 08: Cargo.toml `start_from_attribute`).
Why: A `start_from` pattern `{impl core::convert::From for mysql_common::params::Params}` also matches `From<&[&dyn ToValue]>`, which Aeneas cannot translate (`dyn`), and Charon's pattern syntax cannot express that impl to exclude it (`&[_]` and `&'_ [&'_ _]` fail to parse).
Behaviour: Unchanged: the attribute is an inert tool attribute.

